Strongly recommend Amazon to stop using EMS!
Product five stars, logistics one star, average three stars.
Don't understand why Amazon is sending EMS. Everyone in the industry knows it's unreliable, after all, computers are valuable items!
The order showed expected delivery on the 20th, so everyone waited for three days at home.
Why does it take four to five days to send something from Xiamen to Fuzhou?
This morning on the 22nd, I checked the logistics and finally received it in Fuzhou. I was preparing to happily receive the package when, in the evening, without receiving any phone calls or messages, I checked the logistics and found that it had been signed for midday, with even the status showing it as 'personally signed for.'
I was instantly shocked!
Who am I? Where am I? Is this computer really mine?
Honestly, it's like questioning life, right?
Finally had to go to the pickup point to get the computer back.
The specific reason, in simple terms, is that the delivery guy mixed up the two tracking numbers; fortunately, the package wasn't lost.
I strongly suggest that Amazon don't use EMS anymore, and I definitely won't buy from them again if they start using EMS for their deliveries.
Awaiting supplier's response
The packaging had no labels, so I directly called the supplier and said that there was no label because it was genuine merchandise. If there is any suspicion, they can send some trim pieces to Johnson & Johnson for verification. I also left my license plate number and phone number, promising to receive a text message notifying me to enter my information into Johnson & Johnson's website for warranty. But I haven't received any such messages yet?
The packaging is damaged; time will reveal the quality of the product.
Severe damage to the outer packaging, while the inner box seems new. The manual appears not to be new; it was renovated in September and is stored in stock. I hope it won't be bad by the time it arrives. Could Amazon explain why several customers mentioned damaged packaging while you seem unaffected? Thank you!
Things are good, but platform bureaucracy remains.
The hard drive is of very good quality with an excellent value-to-price ratio, and it's even cheaper than in Hong Kong. It's definitely recommended to purchase if you're not in a hurry and can tolerate the logistics.
But it must be said that Amazon’s bureaucracy remains the same as it was years ago when I swore I would never use it again. You can never track the actual shipping status, and information always arrives weeks later. You can never file a complaint, so bureaucratic!
It has been days since the shipment arrived, but the logistics information still shows that you will receive the goods 10 days from now!
Incorrect image
I thought I would receive headphones like Figure 1, but instead received headphones like Figure 2. Besides the mismatch between the item and the image, what does it mean that the left and right sounds are different?
While the names are the same, please be cautious and also kindly ask Amazon's representative to replace the correct image promptly. Thank you very much.
The worst online shopping experience
After placing the order on September 28th, the system showed it had been shipped, but I did not receive the goods until October 12th.
Checking the status of an Amazon order, the seller did not provide a tracking number, so I can't find where the order is.
So I sent an email to the seller asking if they could provide a tracking number, but received no response for two days.
As a last resort, I contacted Amazon customer service, who revealed the seller's phone number. I called the store, and after a few attempts, the call connected. The seller informed me that the package had been lost and that I could have a new one sent to me immediately.
Although I was very angry, since the computer was urgently needed, I didn't say much to the seller and just asked for it to be sent to me immediately.
So, the next day, I called to ask if it had shipped?
The seller says it's not available yet; it will be shipped in the afternoon.
I called again in the afternoon, and the seller said they would definitely ship it, with shipment after 5 or 6 PM in the afternoon. However, when I called at 7 PM, there was no answer.
On the third morning, I called again to ask if the shipment had been sent out?
May I have the order number?
The seller said they haven't shipped it yet. They told me to order from another place if I need it urgently, and that if not, it will be shipped in the afternoon.
There's nothing I can do; placing an order from another place will take much longer.
All I can do is beg the seller to ship quickly.
Finally, after countless phone calls, I received the computer on October 16.
As for the quality of the computer, I don't know since it was bought for someone else. I'll add a review later.
